,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.744337254,"data":"  Q1  is the window the WHOLE cost?  SPLIT=1 is a window of 1 element, i.e.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.745220189,"data":"      no re-summation at all, which is what a scan does.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.746186606,"data":"      SPLIT=1    329.748 ms  = 592.46x the copy floor\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.747098041,"data":"      SPLIT=256   28.667 ms  = 51.51x the copy floor\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.747761663,"data":"      -\u003e shrinking the window from 256 to 1 buys only 0.09x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.748725081,"data":"      -\u003e a windowless scan would still be 592.5x the floor, so SOME of the gap survives.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":75.749567179,"data":"\n"}
